	abstract = {This chapter introduces the reader to the fundamentals of linear {MPC}. Intentionally light on the formulation, this chapter should serve as a first encounter with {MPC}. The process we followed to introduce {MPC} to new readers is a gradual one. As a start, rough guidelines are provided to allow the reader to choose between {PID} and {MPC} control strategies. Secondly, a modified version of {PID} controller that resembles {MPC} is presented as a concept between {PID} and {MPC}. The proposed {PID} controller has a prediction horizon. Later on, the control horizon concept is introduced and integrated with the suggested {PID} controller. {MPC} is presented to the reader along with the optimization solver that goes along with it. The chapter is concluded by introducing the Matlab Model Predictive Control toolbox.},
